  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 133 PM EDT Fri May 29 2026\n\nBenign weather will persist through at least Thursday as an Omega \nBlock pattern remains locked in. In the upper levels there will be \nlittle deviation with the local area residing along the interface of \nan Upper Midwest to south-central Canada ridge and an eastern CONUS \ntrough. Deep layer subsidence in this regime will generally keep a \nlower column anticyclone in place across the region resulting in \nseasonable temperatures, plenty of sunshine and comfortable humidity \nlevels. A moisture-starved backdoor cold front does swing through \nlater tonight with Saturday cooler and breezier in its wake. \nSlightly warmer weather (similar to the last several days) returns \nby early next week.\n\nEnsembles continue to break down the blocking pattern late next week \ninto the following weekend with increasing humidity and non-zero \nrain chances.",
